# Zod

![zod logo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/colinhacks/zod/master/logo.svg)

TypeScript-first schema validation with static type inference

## Features

- **Zero dependencies** - Just TypeScript
- **Works in Node.js and all modern browsers**
- **Tiny** - 8kb minified + zipped
- **Immutable** - Methods return new instance
- **Concise yet expressive schema syntax**
- **Composable** - Build complex types from simple building blocks
- **Functional approach** - Parse, don't validate
- **Works with plain JavaScript** - No TypeScript required

## Installation

```bash
npm install zod
```

## Basic Usage

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

// Creating a simple schema
const mySchema = z.string();

// Parsing
mySchema.parse('hello'); // => "hello"
mySchema.parse(12); // => throws ZodError

// Safe parsing
mySchema.safeParse('hello'); // => { success: true, data: 'hello' }
mySchema.safeParse(12); // => { success: false, error: ZodError }
```

## Creating schemas

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

// Primitives
z.string();
z.number();
z.boolean();
z.date();
z.undefined();
z.null();
z.any();
z.unknown();
z.never();

// Objects
const User = z.object({
  username: z.string(),
  age: z.number().min(18),
  email: z.string().email(),
});

type User = z.infer<typeof User>;
// { username: string; age: number; email: string }
```

